{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1028672-artifact-troubleshooting","id":1028672,"title":"Artifact Troubleshooting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-08T13:43:49-08:00","id":1028672,"title":"Artifact Troubleshooting","content":"I don't get Artifacts very well, so I thought I might ask some questions here! You guys are great with the crunchy stuff!<br /> <br /> <b>1) Reaching:</b>It says Artifacts can't Reach beyond their Free Reach, which most of times will go for the Instant casting (I am assuming). Can Mages Reach with an Artifact? I know Sleepers and Sleepwalkers apparently can Reach with Imbued Items according to the errata, so how does that work?<br /> <br /> <b>2) Duration:</b> If the Reach is used to Instant cast, then the Duration of Artifacts is always the basic Duration? How does that work when you have Artifacts in 1e that work 'for as long as you wear that item'?<br /> <br /> <b>3) Flaws: </b>Many Artifacts have flaws, at least they had, and this is nowhere to be found in the write-up of the merit. Is this still a thing? I loved the Artifact flaws and how they enhanced the feeling of uniqueness.<br /> <br /> Those are all I have for now! Thanks in advance for all the help!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T14:08:37-08:00","id":1028685,"title":"","content":"The amount of Reach that you have for free depends on the level of your arcana and the level of the spell that you're casting, it can be higher than one.<br /> <br /> I don't remember artifact flaws being a thing so it doesn't surprise me that they're not a thing. You can still build in cursesor whatever though, because not being a thing doesn't mean it can't be a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T14:46:54-08:00","id":1028698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1028672-artifact-troubleshooting?p=1028685#post1028685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The amount of Reach that you have for free depends on the level of your arcana and the level of the spell that you're casting, it can be higher than one.<br /> <br /> I don't remember artifact flaws being a thing so it doesn't surprise me that they're not a thing. You can still build in cursesor whatever though, because not being a thing doesn't mean it can't be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What if you are a Sleepwalker? You don't have Arcana, but you can Reach with an Imbued Item. Could you Reach with an Artifact, or is that a particular trait of Imbued Items?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T15:30:32-08:00","id":1028711,"title":"","content":"I'm also struggling with these rules, even after reading through the Merits and the Imbue Item Attainment. Ultimately I had to come up with my own interpretation - something I <i>think</i> was intended. When calculating the base cost of an Artifact <i>don't</i> use the highest Arcanum, but find which effect has the highest &quot;Arcanum -1 + available Reach&quot; and use that. That way an Artifact that casts Mend (Life 4) with 1 free Reach has the base cost of 4, but one that casts Mend (Life 4) with 2 free Reach has a base cost of 5. The same goes for Imbued Items. Admittedly, the book says absolutely nothing about this, so I could be way off.<br /> <br /> As for the Flaws, I assume you mean the system introduced in Tome of Mysteries. If I recall correctly, it only involved Imbued Items, but having a cursed Artifact is reasonable. I think the old Corebook even had one. Note that the newest edition of Mage had a limited word count and they could only provide very basic Artifact rules. Upcoming Signs of Sorcery (Tome of Mysteries 2.0) will expand on Artifacts and I suspect Flaws may be implemented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 01-08-2017, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:09:39-08:00","id":1028773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gimmisky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1028672-artifact-troubleshooting?p=1028698#post1028698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if you are a Sleepwalker? You don't have Arcana, but you can Reach with an Imbued Item. Could you Reach with an Artifact, or is that a particular trait of Imbued Items?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7593_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7593\" data-vbnamecard=\"7593\">Teatime</a> Sorry, you're doing it wrong, hopefully this clarifies.<br /> <br /> An Imbued Item would have 1 free Reach to use when casting a spell, but the user can apply any number of Reach for the spell that they wish to. Doing so will increase the chances of causing a Paradox which can't be contained. When a Sleepwalker or other non-Mage activates an Imbued Item they roll a dice pool equal to the arcana rating of the spell imbued into the item. So for instance if the item has a 1 dot spell imbued into it then they would roll 1 die (They could roll WP to increase their odds of success though). Mages who activate the Imbued Item would also get to add their Gnosis for free. I assume that the dice pool can be penalized in order to get increased spell factors, in the example I just gave of a Sleepwalker with an Imbued Item that casts a 1 dot spell if he doesn't spend WP he can't spend any dice to increase spell factors.<br /> <br /> An Artifact on the other hand has an arcana rating equal to the highest level effect it produces. So say that you have an artifact that has a 1 dot effect and a 3 dot effect in the same arcana. This means it has an arcana rating of 3 for the purposes of using its effects. For the 3 dot effect it has only 1 free Reach, but for the 1 dot effect it has 3 free Reach. Note that you -can- spend over the free Reach, the reason that they make any mention of that not being the case is for those situations in which an artifact auto-activates. In other words, an artifact never uses its powers for itself in a way that will generate a Paradox, but a user of the artifact can push it beyond those safe limits. The item also has a Gnosis meaning a Sleepwalker who uses it will have a bigger base dice pool than if they were using an Imbued Item because instead of just roll Arcana (+ Maybe Willpower) they're rolling Gnosis + Arcana (+ Maybe WP) which means they can take bigger dice penalties for better spell factors. They also have the ability to attempt to contain a Paradox that might be caused by their use of the artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:26:06-08:00","id":1028785,"title":"","content":"Well... what you said agrees with the Corebook. The thing is, an Item Imbued with a simple Unveiling spell has only a single safe Reach, even if it's created by a Master. I keep wondering if that's intended.<br /> <br /> Oh, and +1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:53:51-08:00","id":1028804,"title":"","content":"I imagine it probably is intended, you can kit out non-Mages with them, which basically makes them the equivalent of a Proximus minus the curse and with a higher level of customization by a Mage. Paradox risk also raises the question of whether or not giving a particular item to someone could count as an AoH or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:58:51-08:00","id":1029067,"title":"","content":"What about duration?<br /> <br /> Many Artifacts in 1e were &quot;works for as long as you wear it&quot; or had lasting effects. How would that work under these new rules? What if I want to make an Eye that is always detecting Magic, or a shield that protects me with Wards and Signs all the time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T08:38:33-08:00","id":1029088,"title":"","content":"Check Enhanced Items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T08:40:27-08:00","id":1029089,"title":"","content":"It seems the system doesn't allow that at the moment. We'll see if Signs of Sorcery changes that. Until then, you have two options:<br /> <br /> 1. Consider what Mrmdubois said.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1028672-artifact-troubleshooting?p=1028773#post1028773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Artifact on the other hand has an arcana rating equal to the highest level effect it produces. (snip) Note that you -can- spend over the free Reach, the reason that they make any mention of that not being the case is for those situations in which an artifact auto-activates. In other words, an artifact never uses its powers for itself in a way that will generate a Paradox, but a user of the artifact can push it beyond those safe limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you cast from an Artifact spend Reach on Advanced Duration, and take a dice penalty so the Spell lasts longer. With a -2 penalty the Spell lasts a day and with a -8 penalty, it lasts a <i>year</i>. At this point it's indistinguishable from a constant effect for most purposes.<br /> <br /> 2. Homebrew it. Unless your players are real sticklers for rules, nobody will object. Use my earlier interpretation as a hack and assume that constant Duration takes 2 Reach. If the Artifact can be activated and deactivated Instantly (like through putting it on and taking it off), add 1 Reach for Instant casting. If you activate the Artifact with a long Ritual, you save a point of Reach. I understand this option might be unsatisfying, if you want to be rules compliant, but CofD encourages altering the rules for your purposes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T08:42:53-08:00","id":1029091,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7593_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7593\" data-vbnamecard=\"7593\">Teatime</a> You don't need to homebrew it, just use the Enhanced Item merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T08:55:14-08:00","id":1029094,"title":"","content":"When Gimmisky said &quot;Artifact&quot; I assumed they meant specifically that. If all magic items are fair game, then you're right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T09:00:10-08:00","id":1029097,"title":"","content":"I would just roll artifact and enhanced item pricing together to get an artifact with persistent effects. Otherwise your option of creating long lasting effects works just as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}